{"id": "plug_power-2026-07-12-008", "date": "2026-07-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": ["plug_power"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["green_hydrogen_cost", "electrolyzer_capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Plug Power to Fuel Expander’s Forestry-Waste SAF Plant in BC", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://media.verna.one/images/resized-1783847280499.jpeg\" alt=\"Plug Power to Fuel Expander’s Forestry-Waste SAF Plant in BC\" /></p>Expander Energy has tapped Plug Power’s GenEco PEM electrolyzers for its Mackenzie Biofuel Project in BC. The MOU aims to integrate green hydrogen production with biomass-to-liquids synthesis to produce sustainable aviation fuel and renewable diesel from forestry wood waste, with FID by 2026 and commercial operation in 2029.", "sources": [{"name": "hydrogen_fuel_news", "url": "http://www.hydrogenfuelnews.com/hydrogen-production-plug-power-to-fuel-expander-s-forestry-waste-saf-plant-in-bc/8576196/", "type": "rss"}]}
